<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Models.</span>
We adopt Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team, 2024</a>)</cite> as the backbone LLM and gte-base <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2023</a>)</cite> as the user multi-source data encoders for our training and inference framework.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation Metrics. </span>Linear probe representation analysis is conducted on all annotated datasets, which is evaluated by AUC (Area Under the ROC Curve <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bradley, 1997</a>)</cite>) and KS (Kolmogorov-Smirnov <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Berger and Zhou, 2014</a>)</cite>) metrics.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2. </span>Main results on six downstream tasks. Performance is measured by AUC(%) / KS. The best results are highlighted in <span id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>;the second-best are <span id="S4.T2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underlined</span>. Our proposed methods are listed in the last three rows.</figcaption>
